{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Molecular.shell_filling_rule","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Molecular.shell_filling_rule","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":39,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.shell_filling_lp_strong_duality_of_certificate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.shell_filling_lp_strong_duality_of_certificate","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L226-L243","doc":"**Claim (iii), derived** from the LP optimality certificate\n(conditional on `ShellFillingLPDuality`, Mathlib `_of_` naming).\n\n`Σ cost_i·x_i = Σ (y₀ + slack_i)·x_i = y₀·Σ x_i + Σ slack_i·x_i\n = y₀·Z + 0`.\n\nEvery step is genuine algebra over the certificate's hypotheses;\nno field of the class states the conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.complementary_slackness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.complementary_slackness","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L222-L222","doc":"Complementary slackness: a site carries assignment or reduced\ncost, never both. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.stationarity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.stationarity","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L219-L219","doc":"Dual stationarity: each site's cost splits into the electron\nchemical potential `y₀` plus that site's reduced cost. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.primal_feasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.primal_feasible","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L216-L216","doc":"Primal feasibility: exactly `Z` electrons are assigned. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.primal_obj_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.primal_obj_def","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L214-L214","doc":"The primal objective is the total assigned cost. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.slack","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.slack","kind":"def","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L212-L212","doc":"Reduced cost (dual slack) at each site. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.cost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.cost","kind":"def","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L210-L210","doc":"Per-site `Φ₁` cost coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.x","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.x","kind":"def","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L208-L208","doc":"Primal assignment variable at each site. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.siteFintype","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.siteFintype","kind":"def","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L206-L206","doc":"The site set is finite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.Site","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.Site","kind":"def","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L204-L204","doc":"Sites available to the `Z` electron trefoils. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.mk","kind":"ctor","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L201-L201","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.toShellFillingRuleContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality.toShellFillingRuleContext","kind":"def","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L201-L222","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingLPDuality","kind":"class","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L176-L222","doc":"**LP optimality certificate for the electron-assignment LP**\n(§3b-cond model class over `ShellFillingRuleContext`, bean\n`qou-kkja`).\n\nClaim (iii) — `primal_obj = Z·y₀` — is *not* derivable from\n`ShellFillingRuleContext` alone, and that is machine-checked below\nby `shell_filling_lp_strong_duality_unconstrained_false`: the base\nclass carries `y_0` and `primal_obj` as unrelated scalars, so a\ncontext with `Z = 0`, `y_0 = 0`, `primal_obj = 1` refutes it.\n\nThis class supplies the LP structure the base class lacks — the\nassignment variables, the per-site cost, and a **dual optimality\ncertificate** (stationarity + complementary slackness).  Claim\n(iii) is then *derived* from those hypotheses by\n`shell_filling_lp_strong_duality_of_certificate`, not carried as a\nfield.  Nothing here asserts the conclusion: the fields constrain\n`x`, `cost`, `slack`, `y_0` and `primal_obj` jointly, and the\nequality falls out of the algebra.\n\nGeneric `[CommSemiring R]` (§7c) — commutativity is used only to\nmatch the `Z·y₀` orientation of the existing statement; no ordering\nand no archimedean structure is required.  Note this is the\n*certificate*, not a proof that one exists: exhibiting `x` and\n`slack` for a given atom is the separate (open) optimisation\nproblem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.shell_filling_rule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.shell_filling_rule","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L153-L170","doc":"**Proposition** ([`prop:shell-filling-rule`]) — resolving\ndeclaration for the `lean.ref` URI\n`qou:QOU.Molecular.shell_filling_rule`.\n\nConjoins the three claims of the aufbau proposition: (i) inner\nshells fill completely, (ii) Hund's rule (the ground state\nmaximises singly-occupied valence sites), (iii) the LP dual\nobjective equals `Z·y₀`.  Each conjunct is a real statement over\nthe model data; the unproved ones carry honest `sorry`s in their\nnamed sub-theorems (see module docstring), not projected\nconclusion fields. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:shell-filling-rule","label":"prop:shell-filling-rule","md":"quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-filling-rule.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.shell_filling_lp_strong_duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.shell_filling_lp_strong_duality","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L142-L151","doc":"**Claim (iii), LP strong duality — stated, not yet proved.**  The\noptimal primal objective of the electron assignment LP equals the\ndual objective `Z·y₀` (`max_y Z·y₀` s.t.\n`y₀ + Σ_n G_{n,s}·y_{n,s} ≤ Φ₁^{(s)}` for all sites `s`).  Strong\nduality for this LP is not yet formalised. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.shell_filling_hund_rule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.shell_filling_hund_rule","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L129-L140","doc":"**Claim (ii), Hund's rule — stated, not yet proved.**  Within the\nvalence shell the ground state maximises the number of singly\noccupied sites: parallel electron trefoils have lower `Φ₁` than\nantiparallel pairs, since the repulsive `ee` crossing (`σ`) is\nminimised on distinct spatial sites.  The `Φ₁` comparison is not\nyet formalised. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.shell_filling_inner_shells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.shell_filling_inner_shells","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L118-L127","doc":"**Claim (i), aufbau — stated, not yet proved.**  Inner shells\n(`n < n_val`) fill completely in the ground state: each additional\nelectron in a partly filled inner shell reduces `Φ₁` more than any\nvalence electron.  The `Φ₁`-monotonicity argument is not yet\nformalised. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.shell_filling_pauli_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.shell_filling_pauli_bound","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L110-L116","doc":"**Pauli occupancy bound — derived sorry-free.**  Every shell obeys\n`occupancy n ≤ 2n²`, from the Pauli hypothesis and the defining\ncapacity formula (genuine algebra, not a projection). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.strong_duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.strong_duality","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L108-L108","doc":"Strong duality equates primal and dual objectives.\n(Needs abstract LP duality infrastructure that does not exist in Mathlib; kept as an honest assumption for models without certificates) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.dual_obj_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.dual_obj_def","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L105-L105","doc":"Definition of dual objective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.dual_obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.dual_obj","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L103-L103","doc":"The dual objective without coefficients. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.primal_obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.primal_obj","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L101-L101","doc":"Optimal primal objective of the electron assignment LP (the\nminimal total `Φ₁`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.y_0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.y_0","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L98-L98","doc":"LP dual variable `y₀` (electron chemical potential). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.singly_le_max","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.singly_le_max","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L96-L96","doc":"All configurations respect the maximum singly-occupied sites. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.ground_singly_eq_max","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.ground_singly_eq_max","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L94-L94","doc":"Ground state achieves the maximum singly-occupied sites. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.max_singly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.max_singly","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L92-L92","doc":"Maximum singly-occupied sites bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.singly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.singly","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L90-L90","doc":"Number of singly-occupied sites of a valence configuration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.ground","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.ground","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L88-L88","doc":"The ground-state valence configuration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.ValenceConfig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.ValenceConfig","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L86-L86","doc":"Admissible valence-shell configurations of the atom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.inner_shells_maximised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.inner_shells_maximised","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L84-L84","doc":"Inner shells are fully occupied due to Φ₁ monotonicity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.occupancy_le_capacity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.occupancy_le_capacity","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L82-L82","doc":"Pauli constraint (structural hypothesis): no shell is occupied\nbeyond its braid capacity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.capacity_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.capacity_def","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L79-L79","doc":"Defining formula `capacity n = 2n²`\n([`def:electron-shell-braid-capacity`]). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.capacity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.capacity","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L76-L76","doc":"Maximum capacity of shell `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.occupancy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.occupancy","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L74-L74","doc":"Ground-state occupation count at shell `n` (the `Φ₁`-minimising\nassignment of the `Z` electron trefoils). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.n_val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.n_val","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L71-L71","doc":"The valence shell index `n_val`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.N","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Neutron number `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.Z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.Z","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Proton number `Z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellFillingRuleContext","kind":"class","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/shell_filling_rule.lean#L62-L108","doc":"Data of the shell-filling claim for atom `(Z, N)`.  All fields are\n*inputs* (model data, defining formulas, and the Pauli structural\nhypothesis); none carries a conclusion of the proposition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}